<title>EGYPT: Yield slips on Egyptian 182-day T-bills.</title>
<headline>Yield slips on Egyptian 182-day T-bills.</headline>
<dateline>CAIRO 1997-08-19</dateline>
<text>
<p>The average yield on Egyptian 182-day treasury bills fell to 8.803 percent at Monday's auction from 8.825 percent at the previous auction on Aug 11.</p>
<p>The new bills, with a value of 1024.6 million pounds ($302.6 million), replace bills worth 771.775 million maturing on Tuesday. The treasury had asked for 700 million pounds.</p>
<p>The Central Bank of Egypt announced the following details (values in pounds, previous auction in brackets):</p>
<p>Maturity date: Feb 16, 1998 (Feb 10, 1998)</p>
<p>Average yield: 8.803 percent (8.825)</p>
<p>Value of bids accepted: 773.600 million (771.775 million)</p>
<p>Value of bids: 1024.60 million (919.775 million)</p>
<p>Range accepted: 8.548-8.845 percent (8.600-8.845)</p>
<p>Range of bids: 8.548-10.200 percent (8.600-10.200)</p>
<p>Number of bids accepted: 90  (52)</p>
<p>Number of bids: 108 (42)</p>
<p>-- Cairo reporting unit +20 2 578 3290/1/ ($ = 3.386 Egyptian Pounds)</p>
</text>
